<article class="env-lemma" id="011Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011Y">Lemma <span data-tag="011Y">12.22.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $0 \to (A, d) \to (B, d) \to (C, d) \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of differential objects. Then we get an exact homology sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to H(C, d) \to H(A, d) \to H(B, d) \to H(C, d) \to \ldots  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0117" data-tag="0117">12.13.12</a> to the short exact sequence of complexes 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \begin{matrix}  0 

&  \to 

&  A 

&  \to 

&  B 

&  \to 

&  C 

&  \to 

&  0 

\\ & &  \downarrow 

& &  \downarrow 

& &  \downarrow 

\\  0 

&  \to 

&  A 

&  \to 

&  B 

&  \to 

&  C 

&  \to 

&  0 

\\ & &  \downarrow 

& &  \downarrow 

& &  \downarrow 

\\  0 

&  \to 

&  A 

&  \to 

&  B 

&  \to 

&  C 

&  \to 

&  0 

\end{matrix}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the vertical arrows are $d$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>